A||||1||Alex4mula||Square fiberglass sub box not good :-(||||8||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||03-31-2001||03:03 PM||||<BR>Well, finished my fiberglass sub box with mix results. The shape fits nicely in the stock location. It is wider at the bottom to hold an 8" sub. It protrude down about 3" from the lowet dash level. Overall shape is kind of square with 4 layers of fiberglass. The walls still flex. Not good for bass reproduction. I will have to add some pieces of metal or MDF to add strength to the walls.<BR>I guess the footwell aplication lacks this problem due to the dome shape. Maybe next time I'll do a dome top.<BR>I used green floral foam to do the shape (glued several blocks) and then covered with masking tape the whole thing and glassed it. Foam came out very easily and I was able to take out even the masking tape from the walls. I recommend this procedure for anyone building one.||||reg||8
Z||000001||stimpy||03-31-2001||08:04 PM||||What I have done on the footwell enclosure I am building for AkursedX is coat the inside and outside with spray-on rubber undercoating. Won't do anything about flex, but should help with resonance. I used Mar-Hyde brand from (where else?) WalMart Auto dept.||||reg||1
